---
// The figure of the RAID-Z room: the map vdev_raidz_map_alloc builds for one
// block, for the visitor's psize, parity, children, ashift and start sector,
// then a read of that block with damaged children. It runs src/lib/raidz.ts
// (the arithmetic and the read path's decisions of vdev_raidz.c) and draws
// with src/lib/raidz-view.ts, which also renders the default layout at build
// time: without JavaScript the page shows that layout and its numbers. The
// reader writes more blocks after it and reads the last one back one step per
// press (DECISIONS.md D23.1); the code is in the room's Source notes, not here.
// What is simplified: DECISIONS.md D4.1.
